<dc:title>Capitol Fourth Concert</dc:title>
<dc:description>&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Since 1979, the National Symphony Orchestra (NSO) has performed on the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/380&quot;&gt;west front of the Capitol&lt;/a&gt; on the fourth of July. The concert is aired by PBS stations as &quot;A Capitol Fourth&quot; and features musicians and vocalists as well as the NSO and the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/144&quot;&gt;Marine Band&lt;/a&gt;. This photograph shows the highlight of the concert, when fireworks are set off from near the &lt;a href=&quot;http://mallhistory.org/items/show/36&quot;&gt;Washington Monument&lt;/a&gt; while the bands play on.&lt;/p&gt;</dc:description>
